WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:21.481
Why are you good at what you are good at? Part is built into you, and part comes from what happens to you. Nature means inherited, biological influences, like genes and brain chemistry. Nurture means influences from outside, like family, friends, culture and life experiences.

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:43.952
Here is how to sort causes of depression and addiction. A parent with the same problem points to genes, so nature. D R D two is a gene linked to addiction, and five H T T is linked to depression. Stressful events, friends praising you, copying a role model, or learning negative thinking all come from outside, so nurture.

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:58.665
Most psychologists say it is not one or the other. Genes may make someone vulnerable. The environment may then trigger the problem. Caspi found exactly this, a gene plus stressful events.

00:00:59.240 --> 00:01:13.681
A question may ask you to define a term, describe the difference, or pick a cause in a scenario and name it nature or nurture. Define questions want one sentence and an example. Always match the right term.

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:35.180
Step one: decide if the question wants nature, nurture, or the difference. Step two: define the term in one sentence, inherited or environmental. Step three: pick a matching detail from the scenario, such as a parent with the same problem for nature, or friends and stress for nurture.

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:52.754
The traps are calling a parent's influence through copying nature, when it is nurture, and defining a term with no example when one is asked for. In a difference question, describing only one side loses a mark. Use the word whereas to contrast them.

00:01:53.880 --> 00:02:11.676
Here is a real exam question. Dawood's friends keep praising his shoes. He ends up with an addiction to shoes. We explain one way nurture could explain it. Two marks.

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:21.067
Step one: define nurture. Nurture means influences from the environment, such as other people and experiences, not inherited factors.

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:35.418
Step two: pick a detail from the scenario. Dawood's friends kept complimenting his shoes each time he bought some. That rewarded his buying, and encouraged him to buy more and more.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:50.996
A tempting wrong route is to say his brother also buys shoes, so Dawood inherited it. That calls copying nature. Swapping shoes with his brother is environment too. Reject the genetic story.

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:55.035
The exam answer. Define, then apply.

00:02:55.600 --> 00:03:05.436
One mark for understanding nurture. One mark for applying it to the friends' praise. This explanation is by olevels dot com, not an official mark scheme.

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:17.805
The most common mistake is calling copying a parent nature. Nature is only what is inherited. If a person learned it by watching, it is nurture.

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:30.263
Now you try. Describe the difference between nature and nurture in depression. Write your answer, then choose Continue to Answer.

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:53.191
Describe nature first. In depression, nature means inherited, biological influences, such as genes. Then use the word whereas for nurture. Nurture means environmental influences, such as stressful life events, from outside the person. Keep each side to one clear sentence.

00:03:53.760 --> 00:04:03.962
A common wrong answer describes only one side. Nature is about genes, and nothing else. A difference question needs both terms, contrasted.

00:04:04.520 --> 00:04:08.817
So decide the term, define it, and pick the matching detail.
